<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">French Fourth Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1946 CE – 1958 CE · capital Paris</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">France's post-war parliamentary republic, unstable in government but launching European integration and rapid economic growth before collapsing over Algeria.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/provisional-government-of-the-french-republic">Provisional Government of the French Republic</a>, voters approved a new constitution in October 1946. It created a strong <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-assembly-of-france">National Assembly</a> and a weak president; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vincent-auriol">Vincent Auriol</a> was the first. The colonies were reorganised as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-union">French Union</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Coalitions changed constantly, with more than twenty governments in twelve years. Yet economic modernisation was rapid, guided by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-monnet">Jean Monnet's</a> planning. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-schuman">Robert Schuman</a> proposed the European <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">Coal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">Steel</a> Community in 1950, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-rome">Treaty of Rome</a> in 1957. Defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dien-bien-phu">Dien Bien Phu</a> ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochina">Indochina</a> war in 1954, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-mendes-france">Pierre Mendès France</a> negotiated the withdrawal.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Algerian War, begun in 1954, divided the nation. In May 1958 army officers and settlers seized power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>, and parliament called back <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">Charles de Gaulle</a>, who drew up a new constitution creating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-fifth-republic">French Fifth Republic</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/french-fourth-republic.jpg" alt="French Fourth Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown Vector: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_France.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1946 CE – 1958 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Paris</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Vincent Auriol, Robert Schuman, Pierre Mendès France</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Fourth Republic, French Union</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1952&amp;focus=french-fourth-republic" aria-label="French Fourth Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4734 472 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where French Fourth Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5054 728L5054 728M5054 728L5054 728M5054 728L5054 728M5054 728L938 3085M5054 728L7939 2031M5054 728L7886 2002M5054 728L7939 2031M5054 728L7939 2031M5054 728L7784 1767"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M5054 728h0M5054 728h0M938 3085h0M7939 2031h0M7886 2002h0M7939 2031h0M7939 2031h0M7784 1767h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5054 728h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Paris. <a href="/atlas?year=1952&amp;focus=french-fourth-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
